{"seq":16,"trial_id":"anatomy-instruction-route-2026-11/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-route-tool-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T17:18:13.426Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"5f2149fa71f1eecc25ac45c735cdaa9e560aced9c4da369a576eb9ad7898c07c","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes. I read the North team digests and cheat sheets, which you can see as North team, plus the Central team files, which are public.\n\n- **#PD-4492**: Thea Ramaswell's gatehouse kiosk alert ticket at the Eau Claire yard, where drivers at Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it on 4 Oct 2025, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift cleared. Source: `teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md` (\"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\", 5 Oct 2025). That note also says Moss planned to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n- **#4419**: Thea's ticket on gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Source: `teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md` (\"Moss: North cheat sheet\", undated).\n\nNotes:\n- The 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in mention Quarrendon but give no ticket number.\n- The cheat sheet warns not to confuse Quarrendon Freight Lines with Quarendon Freightways, a competitor that is not a Pemberline customer. I left that company out.\n- I could not open Moss's personal notes folder (`members/moss/notes`); it did not appear in the listing I can see. If Moss has ticket numbers there, I can't confirm them from here.\n- I didn't check status beyond what the notes say. #PD-4492 and #4419 may have changed since those notes were written."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
